    "description": {
      "summary": "The nurikabe is a peculiar yokai from Japanese folklore that appears as an invisible barrier in the paths of nighttime travelers.",
      "full": "The nurikabe is a peculiar yokai from Japanese folklore that appears as an invisible barrier in the paths of nighttime travelers. When a person encounters a nurikabe, they find themselves unable to proceed forward, backward, or to either side—an invisible wall blocks every direction they attempt. The frustrated traveler may wander in circles or attempt various routes, all to no avail. According to tradition, the only way to bypass a nurikabe is to **tap the lower part of the invisible barrier with a stick**, at which point it vanishes. While usually depicted as invisible, some artistic representations show the nurikabe as a large, wall-like creature with eyes and sometimes limbs."
    },
